1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,641
Part four: Allergies.

2
00:00:03,841 --> 00:00:09,339
The patient's allergies in ThoroughCare must be exactly the same as in PointClickCare.

3
00:00:09,379 --> 00:00:11,424
You add them one by one.

4
00:00:13,324 --> 00:00:17,941
Each allergy in PointClickCare becomes one entry in ThoroughCare.

5
00:00:18,241 --> 00:00:20,634
The allergen goes in Substance.

6
00:00:20,934 --> 00:00:23,994
A category of Drug becomes medication.

7
00:00:24,294 --> 00:00:30,213
The date goes in Date Identified, and any reaction manifestation goes in Reaction.

8
00:00:30,513 --> 00:00:34,127
And you check Critical only when the severity is Severe.

9
00:00:36,127 --> 00:00:39,123
In the assessment menu, open Allergies.

10
00:00:39,373 --> 00:00:42,718
The first question is: Do you have any allergies?

11
00:00:42,968 --> 00:00:51,553
There are three options: Select from pre-defined list, which is recommended. Does not have any allergies. And Enter as free text.

12
00:00:51,818 --> 00:00:56,393
This patient has allergies, so choose Select from pre-defined list.

13
00:00:56,643 --> 00:01:03,671
A table opens: Let's list everything that you're allergic to. You'll add the allergies to it, one by one.

14
00:01:04,994 --> 00:01:07,030
Switch to PointClickCare.

15
00:01:07,288 --> 00:01:13,153
The patient's banner lists the allergies, but you need the details. Open the Allergies tab.

16
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:23,800
Every allergy is listed here, with its allergen, type, category, reaction manifestation, severity, and date.

17
00:01:24,050 --> 00:01:35,259
This patient has seven: COVID-19 Adenovirus vaccine, insulin lispro, penicillin, MiraLax, statins, sulfa antibiotics, and Flagyl.

18
00:01:35,509 --> 00:01:38,633
Each one needs its own entry in ThoroughCare.

19
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:42,760
Back in ThoroughCare, click New Allergy.

20
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:49,782
The Add/Edit Allergy window opens. It has Category, Date Identified, Reaction, Substance,

21
00:01:49,822 --> 00:01:53,384
and two checkboxes: Critical and Active.

22
00:01:55,360 --> 00:02:01,812
In PointClickCare, start with the first allergy: COVID-19 (Adenovirus) Vaccine.

23
00:02:02,074 --> 00:02:04,153
Copy the allergen's name.

24
00:02:04,403 --> 00:02:06,738
Note the category: Drug.

25
00:02:07,115 --> 00:02:11,429
And copy the date: 9/23/2025.

26
00:02:12,771 --> 00:02:19,070
Back in ThoroughCare, click Substance, and open your clipboard history with Windows key + V.

27
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:21,832
Paste the allergy's name.

28
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:29,783
Open the Category list. The options are food, medication, environment, and biologic.

29
00:02:30,033 --> 00:02:32,898
A vaccine might look like a biologic.

30
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:37,698
But always follow PointClickCare. There, the category is Drug.

31
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:41,564
Drug means medication. So choose medication.

32
00:02:44,927 --> 00:02:49,459
Click Date Identified, and paste the date from your clipboard history.

33
00:02:49,709 --> 00:02:55,521
The date is 09/23/2025, the same as in PointClickCare.

34
00:02:55,776 --> 00:02:58,872
Then check Active. The allergy is current.

35
00:03:00,860 --> 00:03:05,499
Next, Critical. In PointClickCare, check the allergy's severity.

36
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:13,556
Check Critical only when the severity is Severe. If it's unknown, low, or moderate, the allergy isn't critical.

37
00:03:13,819 --> 00:03:17,434
This one is Unknown, so leave Critical unchecked.

38
00:03:20,327 --> 00:03:25,091
Then Reaction. If PCC lists a reaction manifestation, copy it here.

39
00:03:25,131 --> 00:03:28,571
This allergy has none, so leave it blank.

40
00:03:28,835 --> 00:03:30,279
Click Save.

41
00:03:32,494 --> 00:03:41,673
The allergy is added to the table: medication, active, not critical, identified on 09/23/2025.

42
00:03:41,927 --> 00:03:45,819
Do the same for the rest of the allergies in PointClickCare.

43
00:03:46,069 --> 00:03:50,713
For each one, click New Allergy, and fill in the details the same way.

44
00:03:50,963 --> 00:03:56,178
When you're done, the list in ThoroughCare is identical to the list in PointClickCare.

45
00:03:56,428 --> 00:03:58,994
That's all you do in the Allergies section.

46
00:04:00,327 --> 00:04:03,110
One more thing about the first question.

47
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:08,276
You chose Select from pre-defined list because this patient has allergies.

48
00:04:08,538 --> 00:04:14,585
If the patient doesn't have any allergies, choose the second option: Does not have any allergies.

49
00:04:14,835 --> 00:04:17,191
Next, the Medications section.

50
00:04:18,594 --> 00:04:20,118
Let's recap.

51
00:04:20,318 --> 00:04:26,087
Choose Select from pre-defined list. In PointClickCare, open the Allergies tab.

52
00:04:26,287 --> 00:04:32,675
For each allergy, click New Allergy, and add the substance, the category, and the date identified.

53
00:04:32,875 --> 00:04:38,708
Check Active. Check Critical only if the severity is Severe, and copy any reaction.

54
00:04:38,908 --> 00:04:43,376
If the patient has no allergies, choose Does not have any allergies.

55
00:04:45,576 --> 00:04:49,592
That's part four. The allergy list matches PointClickCare.

56
00:04:49,792 --> 00:04:54,751
In part five, you add the patient's medications from their pharmacy orders.
